From: Mateusz Jablonski <mateusz.jablonski@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:14:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Align command visit extension with Level Zero 1.35 headers
Upstream-commit: f62ce187bf8fe2920f3549472adf70fd76af9940
Origin: backport, https://github.com/intel/compute-runtime/commit/f62ce187bf8fe2920f3549472adf70fd76af9940

Level Zero 1.35.0 ships the command visit extension in ze_api.h. The
ZE_COMMAND_VISIT_EXT_NAME guard then disables the runtime's experimental
fallback, but this release still uses its pre-specification identifiers.

Use the official type, member, flag, callback, and structure names; retain
fallback definitions for Level Zero 1.34 and accept legacy concrete visitor
structure identifiers. Update the existing tests and add the upstream
legacy-structure regression test.

Backported to compute-runtime 26.40.40196.8 used by openSUSE:Factory rev 29.
Adapted to the inline CommandList::visit implementation and the older graph
implementation; omitted upstream hunks for APIs not present in this release.

Signed-off-by: Mateusz Jablonski <mateusz.jablonski@intel.com>
---
